name "sec:Results"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This section describes the experimental methodology and presents the performance evaluation of the proposed PEAO algorithm.
 It begins with the benchmark functions,
 experimental setup,
 and parameter configuration.
 The impact of the main algorithmic components,
 including the number of subpopulations,
 propagation strategies,
 communication mechanisms,
 adaptive search factor and parallel implementation,
 is then systematically investigated.
 Finally,
 comparative experiments with representative optimization algorithms are presented to evaluate the effectiveness,
 robustness and computational efficiency of the proposed method.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Experiments Setup
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Benchmark Functions
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
A diverse collection of established continuous optimization benchmark functions was selected to evaluate the proposed PEAO algorithm.
 Several of these functions constitute the fundamental building blocks of widely adopted benchmark suites,
 including BBOB and CEC,
 where they are typically combined to construct transformed and composite benchmark problems.
 In this work,
 the original formulations of these functions were considered in order to provide a direct and transparent assessment of the proposed method over a wide range of optimization landscape characteristics.
 
