 The selected benchmark set covers a variety of problem characteristics,
 including unimodal,
 multimodal,
 ill-conditioned,
 weak global structure and non-separable functions.
 Consequently,
 the experimental evaluation examines the algorithm's convergence behavior,
 exploration and exploitation capabilities,
 robustness against local optima,
 and scalability under different optimization scenarios.
 All benchmark problems were tested using dimensionalities ranging from 25 to 150 variables,
