\begin_layout Subsubsection
Speedup Analysis
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To evaluate the parallel implementation,
 experiments were conducted using 1,
 5 and 10 processing threads while maintaining a fixed configuration of 10 subpopulations.
 Table 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "tab:tab14"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

 reports the corresponding execution times,
 speedup values,
 and parallel efficiencies.
 The results show modest improvements in execution time as the number of processing threads increases,
 while the achieved speedup remains close to unity across the examined benchmark instances.
 Furthermore,
 parallel efficiency decreases with the number of processing threads,
 indicating limited scalability of the proposed implementation under the considered experimental conditions.
\end_layout

